e":"38…Bc3","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"38…Bc3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Protects the a3 pawn, which was hanging.","The next best move, 38…e4, would drop Black's winning chances from 68% to 58% (−0.84).","38…Bc3 stops Rd3.","White was threatening Rd3, winning a pawn, picking it up with 39.Nxe5. Bc3 takes care of it.","White answers 39.h4, pushing the pawn storm towards the king, leaving Black with a king with pawns missing from its shelter.","Engine line: 39.h4 h5 40.Bd6 Rd8 41.Ne7+ Kh7 (−2.14)."]},{"ply":78,"name":"39…Bb2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"39…Bb2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Shores up the a3 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 1).","The next best move, 39…Bd4, would drop Black's winning chances from 73% to 56% (−0.69).","39…Bb2 shores up the a3 pawn.","White answers 40.Rd2, attacking the knight on e2, which is undefended.","Engine line: 40.Rd2 Nc1 41.Ne7+ Kh7 42.Rc2 e4 (−2.85)."]},{"ply":81,"name":"41.h4","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"41.h4 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 23% to 13%.","points":["Black answers 41…Nc1: the knight forks the rook and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","Moves a pawn from in front of the king, loosening its cover.","Better was 41.Rd2 (−3.22), which attacks the knight on e2, which is undefended."],"better":"41.Rd2 threatens Rxe2, winning a knight. Engine line: 41…Nc1 42.Rc2 e4 43.Kg1 Rd8 44.Nc6 (−3.22)."}],"opening":{"name":"Italian Game: Classical Variation, Giuoco Pianissimo","eco":"C54","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 12…Ng6: 24 moves in all, 12 by White and 12 by Black.","Theory runs out after 12…Ng6: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}